  "description": "The 2026 election for Texas's 14th Congressional District pits seven-term Republican incumbent Randy Weber against Democratic nominee Thurman Bill Bartie, the former mayor of Port Arthur. The district covers Southeast Texas including Galveston, Beaumont, Port Arthur, and Brazoria County, and has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+12, making it a reliably Republican seat. Weber, first elected in 2012, is a staunch conservative who serves on the House Energy and Commerce Committee, while Bartie emphasizes a 'people over politics' approach and has campaigned on protecting Social Security and healthcare access. The Cook Political Report rates the race as 'Solid Republican,' giving Weber a strong advantage heading into the general election.",
